  "worked_solution": "To calculate $2÷\\frac{1}{3}$, we need to divide each of $2$ wholes into $3$ equal parts, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14128162/assets/291ef5c96846fd1244b9be904da7d56db056befa0758b78c169f24b414d8b96e.png)\n\n \n\nWe get $2\\times 3=6$ pieces in total. \n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n2÷\\frac{1}{3}=6\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
